\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The training-free classical chain (CLAHE, semantic layers, PCA axis, centreline, alignment) recovers the known geometry of the synthetic suite. (a) Belt-axis orientation error per scene, against the $8^\circ $ product tolerance; the two larger errors are the empty diagonal and the curved belt (orange), where a single straight axis is an approximation by construction. (b) Belt-footprint intersection-over-union against the generated belt mask, well above the $0.50$ recovery floor at every orientation.}}{2}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:geometry}{{1}{2}{The training-free classical chain (CLAHE, semantic layers, PCA axis, centreline, alignment) recovers the known geometry of the synthetic suite. (a) Belt-axis orientation error per scene, against the $8^\circ $ product tolerance; the two larger errors are the empty diagonal and the curved belt (orange), where a single straight axis is an approximation by construction. (b) Belt-footprint intersection-over-union against the generated belt mask, well above the $0.50$ recovery floor at every orientation}{figure.1}{}}
