\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Per-class segmentation of the classical core against the four-class synthetic ground truth, each class scored where it is the observable surface. Background/structure, exposed belt rubber and mineral content are recovered at intersection-over-union $0.81$ to $0.96$. Small foreign objects are not isolated by the classical core (per-class intersection-over-union $0.00$): that class is the task the engine hands to its optional learned lane. Dots are per-scene values.}}{3}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:semantic}{{2}{3}{Per-class segmentation of the classical core against the four-class synthetic ground truth, each class scored where it is the observable surface. Background/structure, exposed belt rubber and mineral content are recovered at intersection-over-union $0.81$ to $0.96$. Small foreign objects are not isolated by the classical core (per-class intersection-over-union $0.00$): that class is the task the engine hands to its optional learned lane. Dots are per-scene values}{figure.2}{}}
